       internal. Every type in it had been declared public, so 32 types formed
       part of this package's API without having been designed as such. Nothing
       outside the library used them: no example, no SIPSorcery.Cli, no other
       project in src. BouncyCastleExtensions is in the list for a related but
       separate reason: it was a public static class in the GLOBAL namespace, so
       every consumer of the package picked up its extension methods on
       BouncyCastle types in global scope.

       These removals are real binary breaks and were made knowingly. As with the
       RTSP entries above, <Left>/<Right> are omitted so one entry per type covers
       all nine target frameworks rather than nine copies each.
       ========================================================================== -->
